    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **59 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule for the registration date already skipped weekends but not public holidays. I extended it in the single source of that logic:\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultRegistrationDate.java`**\n- Added the fixed public-holiday set (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Updated `toBusinessDay(...)` so the roll-forward loop also skips any date in that holiday set \u2014 so a date landing on a holiday advances to the next non-holiday weekday (and if that next day is itself a weekend/holiday, e.g. 2026-12-25 \u2192 26th/27th weekend \u2192 28th holiday \u2192 29th, it keeps rolling).\n- Updated the class Javadoc to describe the holiday behaviour.\n\nThis matches the reference `toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` table the tests pin in `AcceptanceBase`, and `Cp47Tests` (the new holiday-business-day acceptance test) passes along with all existing tests.",
